Z||000000||80's BOY||04-17-2000||02:39 PM||||the roll bars are installed and the space frame is cut. it's sounds so simple when you say it, even though all in all the weekend work added up to about 6 hours shop time with the welding and cutting. my suggestions so far with anyone cutting their top out... start with the cutoff wheel for the main part, but do the strongest part of the frame with some sort of sawzall.(this means you, pollock) the corners were too thick and the cutoff wheel wasn't long enough to go through without difficulty. i still did a good clean job without great incident. in other words, i'm not regretting it. now is the time to design an attachment mechanism for the top to go back on. i found a wrecked daihatsu rocky that has a top just like what i cut out. i'm studying this top very carefully. probably will use the hooks and handle mechanism. also someone told me the sunbird convertible seal will fit the front of the fiero. i'd like more info. as for the gaping holes in the back where the top comes off, i might take seam sealer and fill the holes in, and then fabricate a snap on cover using the end piece from a damaged roof panel of another fiero. this will have to be installed when the top is taken off, for asthetics only. as for the frame, it seems to be more stable than before i installed the roll bars. tighter in the curves that is. although the car has a little twist when you try to slalom the yellow stripes, the cool factor is AWESOME!! can you imagine cruising in a full targa fiero?? i love it!! now i need to put the interior back together and get back into action. i just keep having nightmares that when i'm driving, the windshield falls in my lap or the car breaks in half. need...more...sleep...zzzzzzzz<BR>no pictures yet. maybe next week.  ||||reg||4
Z||000001||pollock||04-18-2000||01:55 PM||||Way to go man!<P>Like Chevy Chase said when they were about to do that appendectomy on Spies Like Us, "Cut the sucker!"<P>It will be weeks before i get to mine.  I spent all this weekend under my mustang and bronco.  (Bring on the Ford bashing, my favorite is F'n Old Rebuilt Dodge)<P>Keep us updated, and i'll do the same.<BR>||||reg||6
